{"content":[{"c":["PELEG"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Son of Eber and father of Reu (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.10.25","r":"Gen.10.25","rawR":"Gen.10.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.10.25","value":"Gen.10.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 10:25"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.11.16-19","r":"Gen.11.16-19","rawR":"Gen.11.16-19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.11.16-19","value":"Gen.11.16-19"}],"t":"ref","v":"11:16-19"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.1.19,25","r":"1Chr.1.19,25","rawR":"1Chr.1.19,25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.1.19,25","value":"1Chr.1.19,25"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 1:19, 25"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.3.35","r":"Luke.3.35","rawR":"Luke.3.35","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.3.35","value":"Luke.3.35"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 3:35"},"). During his lifetime, the earth was divided (Peleg means “division” or “watercourse”). Precisely what the division refers to is still debated. Suggestions include (1) the geographical and linguistic dispersion following the Tower of Babel fiasco (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.11.1-9","r":"Gen.11.1-9","rawR":"Gen.11.1-9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.11.1-9","value":"Gen.11.1-9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 11:1-9"},"); (2) dispersion of Noah’s descendants; (3) separation of the people of Arphaxad from Joktanide Arabs (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.10.24-29","r":"Gen.10.24-29","rawR":"Gen.10.24-29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.10.24-29","value":"Gen.10.24-29"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 10:24-29"},"); and (4) the division of land by irrigation canals (the term is so used in ",{"href":"?bref=Job.29.6","r":"Job.29.6","rawR":"Job.29.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.29.6","value":"Job.29.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jb 29:6"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Job.38.25","r":"Job.38.25","rawR":"Job.38.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.38.25","value":"Job.38.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"38:25"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.30.25","r":"Isa.30.25","rawR":"Isa.30.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.30.25","value":"Isa.30.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 30:25"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.32.2","r":"Isa.32.2","rawR":"Isa.32.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.32.2","value":"Isa.32.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"32:2"},"). The origin of the name is usually traced to the city of Phalga, north of the junction of the Euphrates and Khabur rivers."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=GenealogyofJesusChrist_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"GenealogyofJesusChrist_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"GenealogyofJesusChrist_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Genealogy of Jesus Christ"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Peleg","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 10:25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.10.25","rawQueryValue":"Gen.10.25","sourceRefExact":"Gen.10.25"},{"anchorText":"11:16-19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.11.16-19","rawQueryValue":"Gen.11.16-19","sourceRefExact":"Gen.11.16-19"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 1:19, 25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.1.19,25","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.1.19,25","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.1.19,25"},{"anchorText":"Lk 3:35","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Luke.3.35","rawQueryValue":"Luke.3.35","sourceRefExact":"Luke.3.35"},{"anchorText":"Gn 11:1-9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.11.1-9","rawQueryValue":"Gen.11.1-9","sourceRefExact":"Gen.11.1-9"},{"anchorText":"Gn 10:24-29","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.10.24-29","rawQueryValue":"Gen.10.24-29","sourceRefExact":"Gen.10.24-29"},{"anchorText":"Jb 29:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Job.29.6","rawQueryValue":"Job.29.6","sourceRefExact":"Job.29.6"},{"anchorText":"38:2